## Codebase Patterns

- `State.refreshFeeds` owns global feed refresh status transitions for the
  header dot: set `feedSyncStatus` to `syncing` before POSTing
  `/api/feeds/refresh`, clear `feedSyncError`, then set `synced` with empty
  `feedUpdateCounts` on success or `error` with the latest message on
  failure.
- `FeedStatus` exposes `aria-label` for every feed sync state and uses a
  keyed status wrapper so error-only attributes such as `title` are removed
  when moving from `error` back to `syncing` or `synced`.
- Feed update UI state in `src/client/state.ts` now uses
  `feedSyncStatus`, `feedUpdateCounts`, and `feedSyncError` as the source
  of truth. Older `feedUpdateStatus` and `feedsWithUpdates` are computed
  compatibility views, so writers should update the new signals.
- The `items_updated_at` trigger in `src/shared/schema.ts` fires on any
  UPDATE to items rows and sets `updated_at = datetime('now')`. Cache
  eviction tests that verify post-eviction item ordering must NOT use
  `ORDER BY updated_at` for verification queries — use `ORDER BY guid ASC`
  or another stable column instead, because eviction UPDATEs cause
  `updated_at` to change.
- Server-side URL fetch helpers in `src/server/feed-fetch.ts` should share
  `fetchValidatedResponse` so URL validation, DNS pre-resolution, manual
  redirect handling, timeout, and blocked-host checks stay consistent.
- Component image fallback UI should follow the `UserIcon` pattern: use
  `useState` plus `onError` to stop rendering broken `<img>` elements.
- Durable Object feed ingestion should only do post-insert enrichment for
  item rows whose `INSERT OR IGNORE` reports `rowsWritten > 0`; existing item
  rows must not be reprocessed or have their non-null `thumbnail_url`
  overwritten.
- Item fields that must leave the Durable Object should be added to
  `ITEM_COLUMNS` / `ITEM_SYNC_COLUMNS`, then mirrored in both local sync
  item upsert paths: `pull-sync.ts` and `push-sync.ts`.
- Dot component colors belong in global `_variables.css` variables and
  `dot.css` should reference those variables rather than hardcoded fills.
- Node static tests that are bundled and piped to `node --input-type=module`
  should resolve repo files from the runner cwd, not from `import.meta.url`,
  because esbuild stdin/eval wrappers change the module URL.
- Feed bootstrap state is carried by `GET /feeds`; add new feed bootstrap
  fields to the `FeedsResponse` type and mirror them in `remoteAdapter`.
- `State.loadFeeds` derives header feed sync status from canonical
  `feedUpdateCounts`; treat legacy `feedUpdateStatus` as compatibility data,
  not the client state hydration source.

