## 2026-05-01 - US-133
Thread: https://ampcode.com/threads/unknown
- What was implemented: Evict by per-feed size cap on sync cycle.
  - Added `evictByFeedSizeCap(db, cacheStorage?):Promise<{feedsTrimmed:number, bytesFreed:number}>`
    to `src/client/db/cache-eviction.ts`.
  - For each feed: computes current size (text + images) via SUM queries, compares against
    effective `max_size_bytes` (per-feed override or site default via `resolveEffectivePolicy`).
    If over cap, queries items with non-null content/description or cached_images, sorted
    oldest-first by `updated_at ASC`, skipping the currently-open item ID. Evicts items one
    by one (null text, delete cached_images, evict Cache Storage URLs) until under cap.
  - Updated import in `src/client/db/sync.ts` to also import `evictByFeedSizeCap` and added
    `await evictByFeedSizeCap(db).catch(() => {})` after `evictByMaxAge` in `runSyncCycle`.
  - Added 5 tests in `test/cache-eviction.ts`: no-op when under cap, per-feed override
    respected, site default used when no override, oldest-first ordering, currently-open item
    skipped.
- Files changed:
  - `src/client/db/cache-eviction.ts`
  - `src/client/db/sync.ts`
  - `test/cache-eviction.ts`
  - `specs/prd.json`
  - `progress.log`
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - The `items_updated_at` trigger fires AFTER UPDATE ON items whenever `updated_at` is
    unchanged — this resets `updated_at` to `datetime('now')`. Test verification SELECTs
    for evicted items must use a STABLE ordering (guid, id) rather than `updated_at ASC`,
    because the trigger changes `updated_at` on any UPDATE that nulls content/description.
  - `evictByFeedSizeCap` opens the Cache Storage bucket lazily (only when the first batch
    of images needs eviction) to avoid an unnecessary async call when no images are present.
  - The `queryOneDb` import from `local-db.js` was not previously imported in
    `cache-eviction.ts`; it was added to support per-feed text and image size SUM queries.
