- What was implemented: Account-wide cache size cap with eviction and settings UI.
  - Added `defaultAccountMaxSizeBytes:Signal<number>` (default 500_000_000) to
    `src/client/local-first-settings.ts`, persisted in the same `LS_KEY` JSON;
    missing field falls back to the default.
  - Added `evictByAccountSizeCap(db):Promise<{bytesFreed:number}>` to
    `src/client/db/cache-eviction.ts`: queries total text+image size across all
    feeds, evicts oldest items across all feeds until total is under the cap,
    skips the currently-open item.
  - Called `evictByAccountSizeCap` in `src/client/db/sync.ts` after
    `evictByFeedSizeCap` in the sync cycle.
  - Added "Total cache size (MB)" number input to the Cache section in
    `src/client/routes/settings.ts`, bound to `defaultAccountMaxSizeBytes`.
  - Added 4 tests in `test/cache-eviction.ts`: no-op when under cap, trims
    over cap across multiple feeds, skips currently-open item, evicts
    oldest-first across feeds.
- Files changed:
  - `src/client/local-first-settings.ts`
  - `src/client/db/cache-eviction.ts`
  - `src/client/db/sync.ts`
  - `src/client/routes/settings.ts`
  - `test/cache-eviction.ts`
  - `specs/prd.json`
  - `progress.log`
- **Learnings for future iterations:**
  - The `items_updated_at` trigger fires on any UPDATE to item rows (including
    content=NULL eviction UPDATEs), resetting `updated_at = datetime('now')`.
    Eviction test verification queries must use a stable ordering column
    (`guid`, `id`) rather than `updated_at` to avoid ordering flips.
  - `evictByAccountSizeCap` fetches the candidate items list once before the
    eviction loop, so trigger-induced `updated_at` changes during the loop do
    not affect eviction order.
